# OpenTune invariants

OpenTune is a metadata mediator. The Fastify API must never proxy, cache, store, transcode, or redistribute audio or video. The Flutter app streams or downloads audio only from the original provider URL.

## Do not

- Scrape copyrighted catalogs or bypass DRM
- Invent a download from a streaming-only source
- Accept arbitrary user URLs and fetch them from the backend (SSRF)
- Commit secrets or audio/media files
- Implement a later development phase until the user explicitly requests it
- Move to the next phase while the current phase has known blocking errors

## Do

- Prefer official APIs or explicitly permitted endpoints
- Require source + license (+ attribution when required) on every track
- Keep provider connectors behind `MusicProvider` capabilities flags
- Store metadata in PostgreSQL; store downloaded files only on the user device
- After each phase: tests, lint/format, Flutter analyzer/tests, docs, then stop
